Setup Proof (VS Code, Node.js, Live Server)

First, lets see what is VS Code, Node.js and Live Server-:

VS Code: it is a code editor for writing codes.
Node.js: it lets your computer execute JavaScript without needing a browser. It also includes npm, which helps install coding tools and packages.
Live Server: it is an extension in VS Code that refreshes the browser when you save changes.

Set-up-:

VS Code -
Open the official website: https://code.visualstudio.com/?utm_source=chatgpt.com
Download the suitable version for your OS(Operating System).
Install it.

Node.js -
1.Open https://nodejs.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com
2.Download the LTS version, which is recommended for stable release.
3.Run the installer and follow the instructions.
4. Check whether the it is installed properly-
   I. Open VS Code.
   II. Open new terminal.
   III. Type commands-> node -v and npm -v, if it displays version number then the installation is successful.

Live Server-
Open VS Code.
Click on extensions and search live server.
install it.
